      "about-intro": {
        "type": "about-intro",
        "blocks": {
          "8667c0d9-d751-472b-aa4c-dc168b97eba1": {
            "type": "text",
            "settings": {
              "heading_text": "What are ear seeds and how do they work?",
              "heading_color": "#977e57",
              "heading_style": "h3",
              "paragraph_text": "<p>Ear seeds are the oldest healing modality you’ve probably never heard of. Rooted in the principles of Chinese medicine, ear seeds are an ancient tool that may support a broad spectrum of health concerns by way of aiding restful sleep, assisting emotional well-being, helping you to relax, and supporting your immunity, focus, energy levels, and digestion. </p><p><br/>They are a needle-free form of auriculotherapy (the stimulation of specific points of the ear to address physical and emotional health concerns) that have been used in Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) for thousands of years. The seeds were traditionally from the flowering herb vaccaria, but our luxe, modern version uses gold or silver plated seeds that are attached to a clear adhesive sticker. So not only are they known for their healing benefits, but they look incredibly cute too! <br/><br/>TCM teaches that the ear is a microsystem of the whole body, where certain points on the ear correspond to different organs or body parts. Energy pathways (or ‘qi’ or vital life energy) pass through the ear and ear seeds stimulate specific points which send an abundant flow of energy to the related organ or area that needs attention. Think of it like reflexology, but for the ears instead of feet.<br/><br/>They also create continual, gentle pressure on nerve impulses in the ear which send messages to the brain that certain organs or systems need support. The brain will then send signals and chemicals to the rest of the body to support whatever ailments you’re experiencing, releasing endorphins into the bloodstream, relaxing the nervous system, and naturally soothing pain and discomfort. <br/><br/>For more information visit our <a href=\"/pages/how-to\" title=\"How To\">How to</a> page.</p>",
              "paragraph_color": "#977e57",
              "paragraph_size": "1",
              "width": "50%",
              "alignment": "center",
              "align_text": "left"
            }
          },
          "4e079d05-1991-4f30-9123-85d0f2bc8f04": {
            "type": "image",
            "settings": {
              "image": "shopify://shop_images/Acu-Seeds_12791.jpg",
              "width": "50%",
              "alignment": "center"
            }
          }
        },
